          "type": "turn",
          "question": "When does guidance describe antivirals as worth considering for influenza?",
          "answer": "Guidance on the use of antivirals for influenza recommends considering them primarily for severely ill patients. In such cases, observational evidence supports their benefit beyond an outpatient setting (source: National immunization advisory committee and infectious diseases society guidance).\n\nHowever, recommendations differ when it comes to low-risk outpatients. Some guidance suggests that antivirals may be a reasonable option for reducing symptoms, while others find the evidence for their effectiveness in this group to be modest and not sufficiently compelling to justify routine use. There is no consensus on this issue, making it important for individuals to discuss their specific circumstances with a clinician (source: National immunization advisory committee and infectious diseases society guidance).\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
